WEBVTT

00:20.937 --> 00:23.356
- Oh, it worked.
- What?

00:24.190 --> 00:25.859
Is that your phone, Asahi?

00:26.401 --> 00:28.445
No, it's the one I picked up.

00:31.114 --> 00:32.157
Is it recording?

00:32.240 --> 00:33.074
Yes.

00:34.492 --> 00:36.786
I think the camera is working.

00:58.141 --> 00:59.309
Let's see.

01:01.061 --> 01:02.395
There's no one in this town.

01:04.314 --> 01:07.317
Everyone in Tokyo disappeared.

01:14.491 --> 01:16.284
We're in Harajuku, yet there's no one.

01:16.951 --> 01:17.994
Yes.

01:27.921 --> 01:29.172
What's going on?

01:36.805 --> 01:38.348
It's been five days

01:38.890 --> 01:40.517
since everyone disappeared.

01:42.018 --> 01:44.521
You're taking a video again?
What are you going to do with it?

01:45.105 --> 01:46.106
To leave a record.

01:46.815 --> 01:48.358
And why would you want to do that?

01:49.442 --> 01:50.944
Someone might see it.

01:54.155 --> 01:55.490
After that,

01:56.783 --> 01:58.076
we met a certain person.

02:00.745 --> 02:04.582
Then we were brought to that place,

02:06.751 --> 02:09.504
and we work there now

02:16.719 --> 02:17.762
Here?

02:29.357 --> 02:30.608
Are you really going in?

02:45.039 --> 02:47.000
It's pitch black!

02:50.295 --> 02:51.254
Momoka?

02:52.297 --> 02:53.381
Momoka?

02:54.591 --> 02:55.717
Momoka!

04:29.310 --> 04:31.729
Time remaining, 15 minutes.

04:45.952 --> 04:47.203
Kill them all.

04:53.167 --> 04:54.168
Jun…

04:55.628 --> 04:57.380
I can't do this anymore.

04:57.463 --> 04:59.299
We've gone too far to stop.

05:02.885 --> 05:05.013
There's no way we can return
to our original lives

05:05.096 --> 05:06.222
after killing so many people.

05:08.933 --> 05:10.018
You heard me, right?

05:11.853 --> 05:14.272
Anyone who goes against me is a witch.

05:19.360 --> 05:20.528
Please shoot me!

05:22.488 --> 05:23.531
Stop it already!

05:30.121 --> 05:31.581
Let's end this game.

05:38.004 --> 05:38.880
I…

05:39.630 --> 05:41.466
I was confined by you guys

05:42.884 --> 05:44.969
the entire time,
even when the murder occurred.

05:46.095 --> 05:47.847
I'm sure you know

05:48.723 --> 05:50.433
I couldn't have been the witch.

05:54.187 --> 05:57.815
If you aren't the witch,
then there's no need to kill me.

05:58.816 --> 06:02.111
Please cooperate with me
and search for the witch!

06:13.539 --> 06:14.457
Arisu!

06:18.044 --> 06:19.170
Stop it!

06:19.253 --> 06:20.421
Hey!

06:22.507 --> 06:23.841
Now I know.

06:25.385 --> 06:26.844
The reason why you attacked Arisu,

06:26.928 --> 06:28.596
even though
he's the only one with an alibi.

06:29.180 --> 06:31.766
That's because you're the witch!

06:35.019 --> 06:36.020
Arisu!

06:43.611 --> 06:44.695
You…

06:45.321 --> 06:46.364
Are you the witch?

06:54.372 --> 06:57.417
Yes. I'm the witch.

07:18.896 --> 07:19.856
Shoot me.

07:22.442 --> 07:23.734
Do it!

07:30.074 --> 07:33.244
- Shoot him!
- Aguni is not the witch!

07:35.246 --> 07:37.081
This is a Ten of Hearts game!

07:37.165 --> 07:39.959
A game that toys with people's feelings!

07:40.501 --> 07:44.464
It's not a game
where you win by killing Aguni!

07:52.013 --> 07:53.431
You're not the witch.

07:54.640 --> 07:55.600
So why?

07:57.143 --> 07:58.936
That's because you have another motive.

08:00.730 --> 08:02.064
Another motive?

08:04.192 --> 08:05.651
The one you killed

08:06.527 --> 08:07.695
was not Momoka.

08:09.447 --> 08:10.406
It was Hatter.

08:12.074 --> 08:13.117
What?

08:19.582 --> 08:21.417
I found out after I saw your eyes.

08:22.668 --> 08:24.962
It was as if you had given up all hope.

08:26.422 --> 08:29.592
Those eyes.
It was the same as mine that day.

08:31.093 --> 08:32.970
Those eyes after I killed my friends.

08:38.476 --> 08:39.852
You're not dumb.

08:40.645 --> 08:43.189
Yet you wanted to kill everyone
right from the start.

08:44.148 --> 08:45.483
That's not like you!

08:47.360 --> 08:50.947
You must have had another motive in mind.

08:54.450 --> 08:58.120
Ever since I came to the Beach,
I thought it was strange.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.832
If you had these many firearms,

09:02.625 --> 09:05.336
the militants would have gained control
over the Beach a long time ago.

09:06.337 --> 09:08.130
Yet that didn't happen until now.

09:09.757 --> 09:10.841
In reality,

09:11.926 --> 09:14.303
you were not in conflict
with Hatter at all.

09:16.013 --> 09:17.890
Didn't you both actually help each other?

09:20.476 --> 09:22.478
You wanted to make sure

09:22.562 --> 09:25.064
that dangerous people like Niragi
don't go on a rampage.

09:26.649 --> 09:28.234
You tried to hold them back.

09:37.702 --> 09:38.661
You…

09:41.038 --> 09:44.667
Weren't you and Hatter
best friends in reality?

09:48.045 --> 09:49.589
Then, why did you kill him?

09:53.968 --> 09:55.219
For some reason,

09:56.846 --> 09:59.890
you couldn't forgive Hatter
for what he did.

10:02.768 --> 10:05.938
You wanted
to stop Hatter and his crazy ways.

10:11.027 --> 10:13.738
You wanted your best friend
to regain his senses.

10:41.057 --> 10:42.475
Will it continue?

10:44.352 --> 10:45.645
Those games.

10:50.858 --> 10:51.859
I…

10:53.110 --> 10:55.071
will create a utopia here.

10:57.448 --> 10:59.909
For those who have fallen into despair,

11:03.913 --> 11:05.873
if we don't have hope,

11:05.956 --> 11:07.416
we just need to make one!

11:11.295 --> 11:13.297
This will be the land of hope.

11:17.134 --> 11:18.260
That's impossible.

11:19.595 --> 11:20.554
No.

11:24.350 --> 11:25.976
We can do it.

11:33.651 --> 11:35.444
Everyone here

11:36.362 --> 11:37.988
is now one!

11:39.281 --> 11:42.034
We shall unite and gather all cards,

11:43.077 --> 11:45.037
and return to the original world together!

11:57.591 --> 11:58.676
These guys.

12:00.136 --> 12:02.471
They dared
to hide their playing cards from me.

12:24.910 --> 12:25.953
Aguni.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.501
As of today,

12:35.337 --> 12:38.007
I will create a third rule.

12:46.807 --> 12:49.185
"Death to the traitors."

12:56.150 --> 12:57.860
What would you know?

13:06.452 --> 13:07.369
Stop it!

13:23.636 --> 13:24.762
What would you…

13:26.931 --> 13:28.933
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

13:38.734 --> 13:39.735
This way.

13:52.039 --> 13:53.207
Congratulations.

14:08.430 --> 14:09.890
How nostalgic.

14:12.059 --> 14:14.436
This place looks exactly
the same as before.

14:19.900 --> 14:20.734
I'm…

14:23.028 --> 14:24.154
at my limit.

14:27.116 --> 14:29.910
It's getting harder
to control Niragi and the militants.

14:33.831 --> 14:35.457
Let's end the Beach.

14:40.254 --> 14:41.297
End it?

14:43.716 --> 14:45.509
All the members of the Beach

14:46.510 --> 14:50.055
are immersed in the happiness
they found there, aren't they?

14:50.639 --> 14:53.058
Returning to the original world
after we gathered all the cards

14:53.142 --> 14:54.768
was just a big lie you came up with!

14:59.315 --> 15:00.566
Let's end this.

15:03.068 --> 15:06.071
Are you going to betray me?

15:13.287 --> 15:15.497
"Death to the traitors."

15:18.167 --> 15:20.878
The rules of the Beach are absolute.

15:20.961 --> 15:22.421
There's no meaning to the Beach!

15:23.464 --> 15:24.632
Let's stop this already.

15:27.343 --> 15:30.888
We need to aim towards hope!

15:30.971 --> 15:32.389
Stop talking like that!

15:34.475 --> 15:36.310
Just where is the hope within the Beach?

15:40.147 --> 15:41.190
A world like this,

15:43.025 --> 15:44.818
where is the hope?

15:55.287 --> 15:56.246
In the past,

15:58.999 --> 16:01.210
I had trusted friends alongside me.

16:04.505 --> 16:05.881
My hope in them…

16:09.093 --> 16:10.427
was enough for me.

16:27.194 --> 16:28.362
For a king…

16:31.782 --> 16:35.536
There are times where
we have to make difficult decisions.

16:41.125 --> 16:45.170
What a pity, Mori.

17:09.278 --> 17:11.613
I was also someone who killed my friends.

17:13.157 --> 17:15.951
I understand the pain in your eyes.

17:18.412 --> 17:19.997
You killed your friend.

17:22.041 --> 17:24.251
And so you wanted
to kill everyone at the Beach,

17:24.334 --> 17:27.212
because they were the ones
who made your friend go crazy.

17:30.632 --> 17:34.887
Your broken feelings.
The game master made use of them!

17:36.638 --> 17:40.434
- That's why this is a Hearts game!
- Shut up!

17:41.810 --> 17:42.811
Arisu!

17:44.229 --> 17:49.651
If that's true, then Aguni just wanted
to kill everyone regardless of the game?

17:52.112 --> 17:53.113
You're joking.

17:54.281 --> 17:56.617
And we went along with that?

17:59.620 --> 18:03.040
Just who is the witch?

18:04.458 --> 18:05.626
I know who it is.

18:07.711 --> 18:09.338
The identity of the real witch.

18:14.885 --> 18:19.306
You can always see the game master's
characteristics in a game.

18:22.059 --> 18:23.393
In a Hearts game,

18:24.686 --> 18:27.314
it always makes a fool out of everyone.

18:27.397 --> 18:28.732
NATURAL BOTANICAL GARDEN

18:28.816 --> 18:31.568
Difficulty, Seven of Hearts.

18:31.652 --> 18:34.363
A game of betrayal
where you play with people's hearts.

18:34.446 --> 18:35.364
Everyone!

18:38.700 --> 18:41.203
The one that needs to hide is the wolf!

18:42.412 --> 18:43.497
Maybe…

18:45.916 --> 18:48.001
there really was a way to end the game

18:49.962 --> 18:51.713
without killing everyone.

18:54.049 --> 18:55.300
A solution

18:56.802 --> 19:00.722
where no one has to die.

19:02.724 --> 19:05.060
But that's impossible.

19:06.645 --> 19:08.397
We have to hunt down the witch

19:08.480 --> 19:10.732
and burn them
in the Fire of Judgment, right?

19:12.025 --> 19:12.943
No.

19:22.119 --> 19:23.829
There's a witch candidate

19:25.664 --> 19:26.790
that makes it possible.

19:31.295 --> 19:32.212
It is possible…

19:34.173 --> 19:36.717
if the witch is Momoka herself.

19:51.773 --> 19:54.443
Momoka struck the knife into herself?

19:55.861 --> 19:56.737
Yes.

19:58.697 --> 20:00.073
If I were the game master,

20:01.783 --> 20:03.577
I would come up with this idea.

20:10.125 --> 20:11.335
What a joke.

20:12.753 --> 20:14.171
I'm the witch!

20:15.380 --> 20:18.300
You guys want to kill me, right?

20:29.269 --> 20:31.855
Aguni is trying
to take everyone down with him!

21:26.618 --> 21:28.036
Hey, Takeru.

21:32.416 --> 21:33.458
Takeru.

21:34.084 --> 21:36.795
Takeru.

21:39.339 --> 21:40.424
Takeru!

21:48.807 --> 21:51.518
The Beach made him crazy.

21:52.394 --> 21:54.688
You guys made him crazy!

21:58.108 --> 21:59.276
I'm the witch!

22:05.324 --> 22:08.160
I know how to stop Aguni!

22:10.162 --> 22:11.872
I'll get Aguni's attention.

22:11.955 --> 22:13.999
Use the chance
to burn Momoka in the Fire of Judgment!

22:16.001 --> 22:16.835
Arisu.

22:18.962 --> 22:21.048
End this meaningless massacre.

22:26.261 --> 22:27.512
Asahi!

22:30.682 --> 22:31.683
Listen up, everyone!

22:34.061 --> 22:38.482
I'm the dealer of this game.

23:09.846 --> 23:11.223
It was a reverse grip.

23:16.812 --> 23:20.774
Fingerprints with a reverse grip
were found on the knife.

23:30.200 --> 23:31.201
This means

23:32.452 --> 23:34.121
Momoka grabbed the knife herself

23:35.622 --> 23:37.290
and stabbed it through her own chest.

23:45.757 --> 23:47.175
She's the witch.

23:52.264 --> 23:53.598
Why would she…

23:54.891 --> 23:56.560
kill herself for a game?

23:57.602 --> 24:00.730
Was Momoka really the game master?

24:02.524 --> 24:04.276
That girl also said she's the dealer.

24:06.987 --> 24:09.948
So were we just being toyed with by them?

24:12.909 --> 24:15.537
But she's human, just like the rest of us.

24:16.413 --> 24:17.456
Ordinary humans…

24:21.543 --> 24:22.794
The two of them…

24:24.337 --> 24:26.923
They might have been
controlled by someone else too.

24:33.763 --> 24:34.806
Aguni.

24:38.518 --> 24:39.728
Let's just stop this.

24:41.521 --> 24:46.109
Don't let the deaths
of the innocents go to waste.

24:50.405 --> 24:54.409
I understand
how it feels to kill your friends.

24:55.744 --> 25:00.582
But we shouldn't take out our frustration
on those who are still alive!

25:03.293 --> 25:04.836
We are still alive!

25:06.254 --> 25:08.215
We're all facing despair head-on

25:09.549 --> 25:12.052
and fighting until the very end!

25:15.931 --> 25:18.850
Don't look down on those
who are still alive!

25:51.049 --> 25:52.300
The fire is spreading!

25:54.094 --> 25:55.262
Run!

25:58.974 --> 26:00.976
- Move the body to the Fire of Judgment!
- Hurry up!

26:11.903 --> 26:13.154
That hurt.

26:19.995 --> 26:22.163
In the first place,

26:24.833 --> 26:28.336
I should have just burned down the Beach
with the Fire of Judgment.

26:29.296 --> 26:30.130
Niragi…

26:30.213 --> 26:31.298
Niragi?

26:33.592 --> 26:35.969
With this, I'll clear the game!

27:31.691 --> 27:33.401
You guys…

27:33.485 --> 27:36.071
I'll kill all of you!

27:58.343 --> 27:59.260
Aguni.

28:09.562 --> 28:11.523
Three minutes remaining.

28:12.440 --> 28:13.441
There's no time!

28:17.654 --> 28:18.613
You grab her legs.

28:27.455 --> 28:28.998
- Get out!
- Hurry up!

29:23.511 --> 29:24.971
Congratulations.

29:25.054 --> 29:26.973
GAME CLEARED
CONGRATULATIONS

29:34.063 --> 29:38.735
There is no place
where we'll always be safe in this world.

29:43.448 --> 29:45.325
The North Pole, which the explorer saw,

29:46.326 --> 29:48.036
was the true form of the world

29:48.995 --> 29:51.247
without the illusions of civilization.

29:54.209 --> 29:58.213
When all is done,
you simply return to the soil.

30:01.758 --> 30:02.842
This land

30:03.635 --> 30:05.470
is the true form of the world.

30:07.597 --> 30:09.140
I'm thankful to this place.

30:12.519 --> 30:13.436
Now…

30:16.648 --> 30:18.316
I'm freer than I ever was.

30:44.676 --> 30:46.553
I guess this is the end of our paradise.

30:54.894 --> 30:56.354
Everyone died.

31:17.250 --> 31:18.376
Those guys.

31:19.377 --> 31:20.545
I can't forgive them.

31:23.006 --> 31:24.048
Let go!

31:24.632 --> 31:25.466
You can't.

31:28.386 --> 31:31.973
They killed all our comrades!

31:33.057 --> 31:34.058
I won't forgive them!

31:58.458 --> 31:59.542
Let's stop this.

32:01.544 --> 32:03.796
We're still alive.

32:06.299 --> 32:08.134
That's all that matters now.

32:11.012 --> 32:12.096
That's all.

32:13.222 --> 32:14.140
Arisu?

32:15.224 --> 32:16.100
Arisu!

32:34.035 --> 32:35.078
I got it.

32:41.250 --> 32:42.627
I got it.

32:43.503 --> 32:44.545
Arisu…

33:31.300 --> 33:33.011
You're quite persistent too.

33:38.182 --> 33:40.935
I started to think that it's pointless
to collect all the playing cards.

33:41.644 --> 33:42.729
Say what?

33:44.439 --> 33:45.690
But with this,

33:47.066 --> 33:49.736
we've got everything
except for the face cards.

33:52.447 --> 33:56.868
But I wonder what the management team
of the game wants us to see?

34:07.837 --> 34:09.505
- Is it recording?
- Yes.

34:11.090 --> 34:13.718
I think the camera is working.

34:17.972 --> 34:19.265
What's this?

34:20.141 --> 34:22.018
It's a video that Asahi left behind.

34:25.021 --> 34:26.105
Let's see…

34:27.940 --> 34:29.358
There's no one in this town.

34:31.027 --> 34:33.988
Everyone in Tokyo disappeared.

34:36.240 --> 34:37.992
After that,

34:39.202 --> 34:40.912
we met a certain person.

34:43.164 --> 34:46.793
Then we were brought to that place,

34:49.253 --> 34:51.798
and we work there now.

34:56.094 --> 35:00.348
We help with setting up the games.

35:03.976 --> 35:05.269
Are you really going in?

35:15.196 --> 35:20.159
People known as dealers help
to facilitate the games.

35:24.038 --> 35:28.835
Sometimes we join games to act as taggers,

35:30.586 --> 35:33.756
or we act as players
to confuse other players

35:33.840 --> 35:36.175
or to help prepare the game.

35:37.760 --> 35:42.181
But during the games,
we're also being monitored,

35:43.724 --> 35:46.853
and we'll be killed
if we reveal that we're dealers.

35:48.980 --> 35:52.817
Are you recording again?
What are you going to do if they find out?

36:12.128 --> 36:17.091
RISK OF ELECTRIC SHOCK

36:24.807 --> 36:26.601
Is this the dealers' base?

37:17.276 --> 37:18.653
Stop!

37:18.736 --> 37:20.529
Place your bets!

37:20.613 --> 37:22.490
I got a ten-day visa!

37:38.214 --> 37:40.091
Just hurry up already!

37:45.096 --> 37:47.265
DEALER WINS

37:53.354 --> 37:54.438
This is…

37:56.983 --> 37:59.402
So they are the game masters.

38:10.496 --> 38:11.706
Many people have died.

38:14.417 --> 38:16.585
There was a girl
who was around the same age as us.

38:19.422 --> 38:24.218
We prepared the game
according to how our superiors wanted,

38:24.302 --> 38:25.553
then we joined the games

38:27.263 --> 38:29.473
and made it so that the players die.

38:30.766 --> 38:32.059
Because of us,

38:33.894 --> 38:35.855
many people die every day.

38:40.276 --> 38:41.819
I can't take this anymore.

38:45.364 --> 38:49.869
We kill people,
win games, and earn visa days.

38:55.583 --> 38:57.043
We get to live for another two weeks,

38:57.126 --> 38:59.920
but I don't even know
how many people we had to kill for that.

39:02.340 --> 39:03.674
I can't take it anymore.

39:05.634 --> 39:06.719
Momoka.

39:08.971 --> 39:11.474
This is all a dream.

39:14.310 --> 39:15.353
It's all right.

39:17.104 --> 39:19.148
We will wake up from this dream soon.

39:32.495 --> 39:34.580
I want to end everything…

40:05.111 --> 40:06.070
This is the place.

40:43.691 --> 40:44.817
There it is.

40:51.365 --> 40:56.871
RISK OF ELECTRIC SHOCK

43:00.869 --> 43:02.204
Are you serious?

43:12.464 --> 43:14.049
You actually found this place.

43:21.015 --> 43:23.309
As expected
from someone I have high hopes for.

43:26.770 --> 43:28.022
We meet again.

43:30.983 --> 43:32.067
You guys.

43:34.695 --> 43:38.115
Thanks to you guys, I have
all the numbered playing cards with me.

43:39.241 --> 43:40.200
Thank you.

43:42.369 --> 43:44.038
How did you discover this place?

43:47.041 --> 43:49.668
It took me some time to realize
that this is actually

43:50.377 --> 43:52.046
the route map of a subway station.

44:08.562 --> 44:10.731
What happens
when we collect all the playing cards?

44:11.523 --> 44:15.069
I thought I would know the answer
after I came here.

44:16.612 --> 44:19.198
But there's only one thing I discovered.

44:20.491 --> 44:22.826
They are not game masters.

44:24.286 --> 44:25.120
Right.

44:26.372 --> 44:30.834
Judging from the fact that
they were all killed after our victory.

44:31.502 --> 44:34.421
They're humans like us,
and on top of that,

44:36.423 --> 44:37.591
there's someone above them.

44:45.474 --> 44:47.893
Just who could they be?

44:49.520 --> 44:50.354
Who knows?

44:51.689 --> 44:52.940
They might be aliens.

44:55.651 --> 44:56.694
Or even God himself.

45:05.411 --> 45:08.122
SPECIAL URGENT BROADCAST

45:12.042 --> 45:15.421
Congratulations to all players.

45:19.133 --> 45:20.259
What?

45:21.677 --> 45:22.803
Interesting.

45:26.932 --> 45:27.850
Mira.

45:30.519 --> 45:32.187
With the exception of the face card games,

45:33.105 --> 45:35.441
all of you have cleared
all the numbered games thus far

45:36.024 --> 45:37.776
and emerged the victors.

45:38.902 --> 45:41.613
A sweet victory you've grasped

45:41.697 --> 45:44.116
by sacrificing numerous lives.

45:49.163 --> 45:54.376
I wonder how many
of your comrades have died?

45:59.548 --> 46:01.008
Try remembering…

46:03.719 --> 46:05.512
those that were shot dead with a gun.

46:08.891 --> 46:10.726
That girl you burned alive.

46:15.230 --> 46:20.319
Those struck with the lasers
and those that drowned.

46:24.907 --> 46:26.950
Those whose heads were blown off.

46:27.659 --> 46:29.203
Those comrades of yours.

46:32.164 --> 46:34.291
The despair you've felt so far

46:35.626 --> 46:39.213
and those dying moments
that you can never forget.

46:42.466 --> 46:46.053
I'm extremely touched!

46:52.184 --> 46:54.102
All of you players,

46:55.229 --> 46:59.608
we would like to give you a present.

47:00.734 --> 47:02.361
Are you returning us
to the original world?

47:05.781 --> 47:07.366
There will be new games!

47:10.285 --> 47:11.745
Let's play games together.

47:11.829 --> 47:13.997
You'll fight for face cards!

47:15.165 --> 47:16.458
New games?

47:18.043 --> 47:19.628
I don't dislike the idea.

47:21.672 --> 47:26.009
We've still got many more
wonderful games prepared for all of you,

47:26.760 --> 47:28.220
so look forward to it!

47:30.681 --> 47:31.974
This woman.

47:32.891 --> 47:34.309
Is she the game master?

47:36.144 --> 47:38.272
I'd rather see an alien
appear on the screen.

47:39.565 --> 47:44.903
The next stage will commence
tomorrow at noon.

47:46.738 --> 47:50.492
Let's have some fun together!

47:52.202 --> 47:53.954
So we have to fight again.

47:55.539 --> 47:56.373
Yes.

47:58.458 --> 47:59.835
But one thing is different.

48:03.463 --> 48:05.716
We're finally seeing our target.

49:33.637 --> 49:35.430
We'll definitely find our answers there.

51:56.029 --> 51:58.949
Subtitle translation by: Qianni Lu
